al=true, all riskFlags=false, evidenceSegmentIds cite actual segments containing the independent educational explanation. For reject: set at least one relevant riskFlags=true and cite actual supporting source segments. If educational=false because the source does not substantively explain the candidate, set unsupported_topic=true; absence of educational support is itself a policy reason. Never return reject with every risk flag false; educational can describe whether any reasoning exists but does not override the risk. For uncertain risk or insufficient context use ambiguous, which blocks the entire publication handoff. Segment IDs must refer to supplied sourceSegments. Never fabricate evidence or require that generic words are unsafe merely because the source has private names."},{role:"user",content:JSON.stringify($json)} ] }) }}

